  "concept": {
    "name": "lens-composition",
    "lens": "composition",
    "fragment": "LENS \"composition\": the drawing's STRUCTURE becomes the terrain literally. Start from ANALYSIS.composition. The main mass becomes the highest land, placed where it sits in the frame; the flow lines become the path and the ridges, running the same way; the negative space becomes void (bays and gaps cut into the island) or open ground; symmetry or its absence decides \"symmetric\" versus an asymmetric shaper; scale cues decide how big the figure stands against the land. Choose the shaper and its params as a transcription: peak, center, from, ratio, split, turns and hand must be read off the frame positions in the analysis (x left to right 0..1, z top to bottom 0..1). Map picture to plan this way: the top of the frame is the far rim (row 0), the bottom is the near rim (row 11). Lighting follows ANALYSIS.palette.value_structure: where the lights and darks fall becomes where sun and shadow fall, and a high-key or low-key picture sets ambient. The figure stands at the focal point and its pose repeats the drawing's main gesture line. Palette follows the value map: the surfaces are ranked by value as the picture's areas are (the emptiest area becomes the palest surface, the densest the darkest), with the piece's accent hue kept for the focal point and its threshold. Props mark the structure: posts along a flow line, a gap where the negative space opens, a counterweight at the second mass."
